  "result": "Analyzed season 1's trip data: yellowtail essentially never appear on HD_AM/HD_PM/twilight trips, concentrate heavily on THREE_QUARTER/OVERNIGHT/DAY_1_5, with a strong Oct\u2013Nov fall window (day_1_5 ypa 4.17 vs summer's 0.2\u20130.5) and a weak-but-real CUTI/SST signal (trailing 14-day CUTI vs catch: -0.30; trailing 7-day SST: +0.25) supporting the upwelling-relaxation thesis, plus large boat-to-boat variance within the same window.\n\nWrote all of this to `notes.md` as the plan for nightly decisions: avoid half-day/twilight classes, concentrate budget/PTO on day_1.5/overnight trips in the Oct\u2013Nov window (start watching trailing CUTI/SST by mid-Sept for the 14-day PTO lead time), use CUTI/SST trend as a timing tiebreaker not a hard gate, and don't trust the default `pick_boat` blindly given the boat-level spread. Left `strategy.py` as no-op since this is only one season of noisy data.",
